insert into recipes (slug, title, summary, body, verified_on) values ('daily-web-game', 'Casual or daily web game that survives viral spikes', 'A game that runs in the browser with one shared puzzle or question a day: players vote or answer, see live crowd numbers, keep streaks and share their result. Static pages on Cloudflare Workers, vote counts and streaks in Upstash Redis, every vote stored in Neon Postgres, and live numbers from one cached results endpoint instead of a realtime service.', '{"slug":"daily-web-game","title":"Casual or daily web game that survives viral spikes","summary":"A game that runs in the browser with one shared puzzle or question a day: players vote or answer, see live crowd numbers, keep streaks and share their result. Static pages on Cloudflare Workers, vote counts and streaks in Upstash Redis, every vote stored in Neon Postgres, and live numbers from one cached results endpoint instead of a realtime service.","matches":["daily game","web game","browser game","daily puzzle","daily question","puzzle game","word game","trivia","voting game","guessing game","wordle","game","games","leaderboard","streaks"],"fitsWhen":["The game runs in a web browser and a round is short (seconds to a few minutes).","Everyone plays the same puzzle or question each day, so most reads are the same for every player.","Players share results, so traffic can jump from hundreds to tens of thousands in a day."],"notFor":["Games built in an engine (Unity, Unreal, Godot), console or 3D games, or phone games: Cuely doesn''t cover those.","Fast real-time multiplayer (shooters, racing, anything that needs an authoritative game server and matchmaking).","Games that sell items or subscriptions inside an iOS or Android app: the stores'' in-app purchase rules apply (see the mobile-subscription-app recipe)."],"stack":[{"category":"hosting","tool":"cloudflare-workers","why":"Static assets are free and unlimited, so a viral day of page loads costs nothing, and Workers Paid ($5/month) includes 10 million API requests a month, then $0.30 per million. Move to Paid before you share the game: on Free, requests past 100,000 a day get error 1027.","alternatives":[{"tool":"vercel","when":"You build it in Next.js and want Vercel''s tooling: Pro ($20/month) has a flat-rate CDN, and a cached results response doesn''t run your function. Hobby is non-commercial and stops for 30 days once you pass 1M CDN requests a month."}]},{"category":"kv","tool":"upstash-redis","why":"Atomic counters for the tally, SET with NX to stop double votes, sorted sets for leaderboards and expiring keys for streaks, at up to 10,000 commands a second, over HTTP from Workers.","alternatives":[{"tool":"cloudflare-durable-objects","when":"You want everything on Cloudflare and to push results over WebSockets; you write the counting code yourself and split counters across objects past 1,000 requests a second."},{"tool":"redis-cloud","when":"You''d rather pay a flat price by memory size than per command."}]},{"category":"database","tool":"neon","why":"The durable record: every vote, each day''s question and final results, in Postgres you can query and recompute streaks from. Its serverless driver connects from Workers over HTTP, and scale-to-zero keeps quiet days free.","alternatives":[{"tool":"supabase","when":"You also want its auth and storage from one dashboard; free projects pause after a week with no activity."}]},{"category":"realtime","tool":"cached-polling","why":"Every player needs the same numbers, so serve them from one endpoint cached for 5 seconds and poll it while the results screen is open. A spike adds cheap cached requests, not connections.","alternatives":[{"tool":"supabase-realtime","when":"You need updates under a second and expect at most 200 players at once on Free (500 on Pro)."},{"tool":"ably","when":"You need pushed updates with delivery guarantees and can pay by monthly active users (500 free, then from $29/month for 1,000)."}]},{"category":"auth","tool":"better-auth","why":"Start with no sign-in: an anonymous player id kept in the browser. When players want streaks on more than one device, add Better Auth (its anonymous plugin lets a guest upgrade to an account); users stay in your Neon database with no per-user fees.","alternatives":[{"tool":"clerk","when":"You want prebuilt sign-in screens; free up to 50,000 retained users."}],"optional":true},{"category":"monitoring","tool":"sentry","why":"Error alerts on the vote and results endpoints, so you hear about a failure on the viral day, not the day after.","alternatives":[{"tool":"better-stack","when":"You also want an uptime check on the results endpoint."}]},{"category":"analytics","tool":"posthog","why":"Daily players, how many come back the next day, and which shares bring new players.","alternatives":[{"tool":"plausible","when":"Page and referrer counts are enough."}],"optional":true}],"steps":[{"title":"Decide when the day starts, who a player is and how votes are counted","detail":"Make three decisions before you design the tables and keys: when a day starts, how you know a player, and how you stop double votes.","actions":["Pick one day boundary for everyone (midnight UTC is simplest, and Cron Triggers run on UTC) and show the countdown in the player''s local time.","Use an anonymous player id: a random id created in the browser on first visit and kept in localStorage. Don''t ask for sign-in to play.","Make the rule ''one vote per player per day'', enforced on the server with SET NX in Redis and a primary key in Postgres, never only in the browser.","Write the first 30 days of questions before launch; a daily game that skips a day loses its streak players."],"check":"You can say, in one sentence each, when a day starts, what a player id is, and what happens on a second vote.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/cron-triggers/"]},{"title":"Create the Worker with static assets","detail":"The game page, scripts and images are static assets, which are free and unlimited. Only /api/* runs your code.","actions":["Create a Workers project and put the game''s HTML, JS and images in a public folder served as static assets.","Send only /api/vote and /api/results to the Worker script; everything else is a file.","Upgrade the account to Workers Paid ($5/month) before you share the game anywhere."],"commands":["npm create cloudflare@latest -- daily-game","cd daily-game && npm i @upstash/redis @neondatabase/serverless","npx wrangler deploy"],"files":[{"path":"wrangler.jsonc","contents":"{\n  \"name\": \"daily-game\",\n  \"main\": \"src/index.ts\",\n  \"compatibility_date\": \"2026-11-01\",\n  \"assets\": { \"directory\": \"./public\" },\n  // Roll the day over at midnight UTC (step 6).\n  \"triggers\": { \"crons\": [\"0 0 * * *\"] }\n}\n"}],"check":"The deployed URL serves the game page, and the Workers dashboard counts requests only for /api calls, not page loads.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/get-started/guide/","https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/","https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/"]},{"title":"Set up Upstash Redis and the Postgres tables","detail":"Redis holds what changes every second (tallies, who voted today, streaks). Postgres holds what you must never lose (every vote, every question, final results).","actions":["Create an Upstash Redis database in the region closest to most players and switch it to pay as you go with a monthly budget before launch.","Add UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL, UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN and DATABASE_URL as Worker secrets with `npx wrangler secret put`.","Create a Neon project and run the schema below.","Key names in Redis: q:{day} (today''s question), voted:{day}:{player} (dedupe, expires after 2 days), tally:{day} (a hash of choice to count), streak:{player} (last day and count), rl:{ip} (rate limit, expires after 60 seconds)."],"files":[{"path":"db/001_game.sql","contents":"create table questions (\n  day date primary key,\n  prompt text not null,\n  choices text[] not null check (array_length(choices, 1) between 2 and 6)\n);\n\n-- Every vote, once per player per day.\ncreate table votes (\n  day date not null references questions(day),\n  player_id text not null,\n  choice text not null,\n  created_at timestamptz not null default now(),\n  primary key (day, player_id)\n);\ncreate index votes_by_player on votes (player_id, day desc);\n\n-- Copied from Redis when the day ends.\ncreate table final_results (\n  day date primary key references questions(day),\n  tally jsonb not null,\n  total integer not null\n);\n"}],"check":"Inserting the same (day, player_id) twice fails on the primary key, and the Worker can read and write a test key in Redis.","docs":["https://upstash.com/docs/redis/sdks/ts/deployment","https://neon.com/docs/guides/cloudflare-workers"]},{"title":"Write the vote endpoint","detail":"Count in Redis and answer the player at once; write the durable row after the response with waitUntil.","actions":["Rate-limit by IP with a short-lived counter (INCR plus EXPIRE 60), or Upstash''s @upstash/ratelimit, so one script can''t stuff the tally.","Validate the player id format and that the choice is one of today''s choices.","SET voted:{day}:{player} with NX; if it already exists, don''t count again.","HINCRBY tally:{day} {choice} 1, then update the streak (a last day of yesterday means +1, anything older resets to 1).","Insert the vote into Postgres inside ctx.waitUntil, with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING."],"files":[{"path":"src/index.ts","contents":"import { Redis } from \"@upstash/redis/cloudflare\";\nimport { neon } from \"@neondatabase/serverless\";\n\nexport interface Env {\n  UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL: string;\n  UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN: string;\n  DATABASE_URL: string;\n}\n\nconst dayOf = (d = new Date()) => d.toISOString().slice(0, 10); // the game day, in UTC\nconst yesterday = () => dayOf(new Date(Date.now() - 86_400_000));\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(req: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<Response> {\n    const redis = Redis.fromEnv(env);\n    const { pathname } = new URL(req.url);\n    if (pathname === \"/api/vote\" && req.method === \"POST\") return vote(req, env, ctx, redis);\n    if (pathname === \"/api/results\") return results(req, ctx, redis);\n    return new Response(\"Not found\", { status: 404 });\n  },\n};\n\nasync function vote(req: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext, redis: Redis) {\n  const ip = req.headers.get(\"cf-connecting-ip\") ?? \"unknown\";\n  const hits = await redis.incr(`rl:${ip}`);\n  if (hits === 1) await redis.expire(`rl:${ip}`, 60);\n  if (hits > 30) return new Response(\"Slow down\", { status: 429 });\n\n  const { playerId, choice } = (await req.json()) as { playerId: string; choice: string };\n  const day = dayOf();\n  const q = await redis.get<{ choices: string[] }>(`q:${day}`);\n  if (!q || !q.choices.includes(choice) || !/^[A-Za-z0-9-]{16,64}$/.test(playerId)) {\n    return new Response(\"Bad vote\", { status: 400 });\n  }\n\n  // One vote per player per day.\n  const first = await redis.set(`voted:${day}:${playerId}`, choice, { nx: true, ex: 172_800 });\n  if (!first) return Response.json({ ok: true, alreadyVoted: true });\n\n  await redis.hincrby(`tally:${day}`, choice, 1);\n  const s = await redis.hgetall<{ last: string; count: number }>(`streak:${playerId}`);\n  const count = s?.last === yesterday() ? Number(s.count) + 1 : 1;\n  await redis.hset(`streak:${playerId}`, { last: day, count });\n\n  // The durable record, written after the player has their answer.\n  const sql = neon(env.DATABASE_URL);\n  ctx.waitUntil(sql`insert into votes (day, player_id, choice) values (${day}, ${playerId}, ${choice}) on conflict do nothing`);\n  return Response.json({ ok: true, streak: count });\n}\n\nasync function results(req: Request, ctx: ExecutionContext, redis: Redis) {\n  // One cached answer per Cloudflare location, refreshed every 5 seconds.\n  const key = new Request(new URL(\"/api/results\", req.url).toString());\n  const hit = await caches.default.match(key);\n  if (hit) return hit;\n  const day = dayOf();\n  const tally = (await redis.hgetall<Record<string, number>>(`tally:${day}`)) ?? {};\n  const total = Object.values(tally).reduce((a, b) => a + Number(b), 0);\n  const percent = Object.fromEntries(\n    Object.entries(tally).map(([k, v]) => [k, total ? Math.round((Number(v) / total) * 1000) / 10 : 0]),\n  );\n  const res = Response.json({ day, total, percent }, { headers: { \"Cache-Control\": \"public, max-age=5\" } });\n  ctx.waitUntil(caches.default.put(key, res.clone()));\n  return res;\n}\n"}],"check":"Voting twice from the same player id leaves the tally unchanged, and the votes table gets exactly one row.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/context/","https://upstash.com/docs/redis/sdks/ratelimit-ts/overview","https://neon.com/docs/serverless/serverless-driver"]},{"title":"Show live percentages by polling the cached endpoint","detail":"The results endpoint caches one answer per Cloudflare location for 5 seconds (the Cache API doesn''t replicate between locations), so heavy polling reaches Redis only a few times a second.","actions":["After a player votes, show the percentages and poll /api/results every 5 seconds.","Poll only while the tab is visible (document.visibilityState) and stop after a few minutes on the page.","Never put anything player-specific (their own vote or streak) in the shared results response; return those from the vote call instead."],"files":[{"path":"public/results.js","contents":"export function watchResults(render) {\n  const stopAt = Date.now() + 3 * 60_000;\n  async function tick() {\n    if (document.visibilityState === \"visible\") {\n      const res = await fetch(\"/api/results\");\n      if (res.ok) render(await res.json());\n    }\n    if (Date.now() < stopAt) setTimeout(tick, 5000);\n  }\n  tick();\n}\n"}],"check":"With the results screen open in two browsers, a vote in one shows in the other within about 10 seconds.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/cache/"]},{"title":"Roll the day over on a schedule","detail":"A Cron Trigger at midnight UTC loads the new question and saves yesterday''s final tally, so the game never depends on someone being awake.","actions":["Add a scheduled() handler that reads the new day''s question from Postgres and writes it to q:{day} in Redis.","In the same run, copy yesterday''s tally hash into final_results in Postgres.","If no question exists for the new day, report it to Sentry and show a friendly ''back tomorrow'' page rather than an error."],"check":"Running the scheduled handler locally for a test date loads that day''s question and writes the previous day''s final_results row.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/cron-triggers/"]},{"title":"Make sharing the growth loop","detail":"Players share a short text result with a link. Most new players arrive through these shares, and the text costs nothing to generate.","actions":["Build the share text in the browser: the game''s name and day number, the player''s pick, how much of the crowd agreed, the streak, and the link.","Call navigator.share() from the Share button where the browser supports it, and fall back to navigator.clipboard.writeText() with a ''Copied'' message. Both need HTTPS.","Give each day its own page with an og:image, made once when you write the question and saved as a static asset, so link previews never run code.","Keep each past day''s results page up, since late clicks on shared links land there."],"check":"Pasting a shared link in a chat app shows the day''s preview image, and the Share button works on a phone and on a desktop browser.","docs":["https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/share","https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Clipboard/writeText"]},{"title":"Get ready for the viral day","detail":"Every free plan in this stack stops or errors at its cap. Set the plans, caps and alerts before the spike, not during it.","actions":["Confirm Workers Paid is on.","Confirm Upstash is on pay as you go with a budget, and Neon''s compute has a maximum size set.","Add Sentry to the Worker and alert on a jump in errors for /api/vote.","Send a few thousand test votes from a script against a preview deployment and check that the tally, the votes table and the cached results agree."],"check":"A test of a few thousand votes in a minute finishes with no errors, matching counts in Redis and Postgres, and a results endpoint that still answers from cache.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/","https://upstash.com/pricing/redis"]}],"bestPractices":["Count in Redis, store in Postgres: the tally is fast and can be rebuilt; the votes table is the truth.","Serve everything that''s the same for every player from cache, and keep per-player answers out of shared responses.","Let people play without signing in; offer sign-in only to keep streaks across devices.","Keep past days'' results as permanent pages, since shared links keep arriving for days.","Write questions weeks ahead and keep a few spares for a day you can''t."],"pitfalls":["Counting with SELECT count(*) on every page view: under a spike, the database becomes the bottleneck.","Keeping the tally in Cloudflare KV or Vercel Global Config: both are built for rare writes (KV allows 1 write per second per key).","Opening a WebSocket per player for numbers that change every few seconds: free realtime plans allow connections in the hundreds.","Launching on a free plan that stops at its cap: Workers Free errors after 100,000 requests a day; Vercel Hobby stops for 30 days past its limits.","Trusting the browser to prevent double votes: enforce it on the server.","A server-side day boundary in local time that nobody wrote down: players in different time zones see different days."],"complianceNotes":["If the game is aimed at children under 13 in the US, COPPA applies before you collect any identifier; get advice before launch.","An anonymous player id and analytics cookies can still be personal data under GDPR for EU players; say what you store in a privacy policy and ask for consent where analytics needs it.","Don''t keep IP addresses longer than the rate limit needs."],"catches":[{"text":"Workers Free has a daily limit of 100,000 requests; past it Cloudflare returns error 1027 (or skips your Worker if the route fails open). Workers Paid is $5/month with 10M requests included, then $0.30 per million.","source":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/","verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"},{"text":"Requests to static assets on Workers are free and unlimited; only requests that run your Worker script are billed.","source":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/","verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"},{"text":"Upstash Redis Free is 500K commands a month; pay as you go is $0.20 per 100K with a budget you set, and every plan allows up to 10,000 commands a second.","source":"https://upstash.com/pricing/redis","verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"},{"text":"Cloudflare KV allows 1 write per second to the same key, and changes can take 60 seconds or more to show in other locations, so it can''t hold a live tally.","source":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/concepts/how-kv-works/","verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"},{"text":"On Vercel Hobby, going over the included usage (1M CDN requests a month) means waiting 30 days to use that feature again. Pro has a flat-rate CDN, and a cached function response doesn''t run the function.","source":"https://vercel.com/docs/plans/hobby","verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"}],"costOverrides":{"cloudflare-workers":{"monthly":5,"basis":"Workers Paid from launch day ($5/month, 10M requests included, then $0.30 per million): Free stops at 100,000 requests a day."}},"costNotes":["Steady state at 1,000 daily players: about $5/month, all of it Workers Paid; Upstash, Neon, Sentry and PostHog stay on their free plans.","A viral day of 100,000 players who each vote once and watch results for 2 minutes (one poll every 5 seconds): page loads are static assets (free), and 100,000 votes + 2.4M polls is about 2.5M Worker requests, a quarter of Workers Paid''s 10M a month (then $0.30 per million).","Upstash on that day: about 6 commands per vote (rate limit, today''s question, dedupe, tally, streak read and write) is 600K, and the 5-second cache keeps results reads small. At $0.20 per 100K that''s about $1.20 to $1.50 for the day on pay as you go.","Neon on that day: 100,000 small inserts sent after each response is light work; watch compute hours (Free has 100 CU-hours a month per project)."],"verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"}'::jsonb, '2026-11-09')
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'hosting', 'cloudflare-workers', false);
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'kv', 'upstash-redis', false);
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'database', 'neon', false);
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'realtime', 'cached-polling', false);
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'auth', 'better-auth', true);
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'monitoring', 'sentry', false);
insert into recipe_tools (recipe_slug, category, tool_slug, optional) values ('daily-web-game', 'analytics', 'posthog', true);
insert into recipes (slug, title, summary, body, verified_on) values ('developer-api', 'API or developer tool that other developers pay to call', 'A paid API that developers call with keys: a dashboard where they sign up, create keys and see usage, an API that checks the key and a per-key rate limit on every request, and usage reported to Stripe for metered billing. It runs on Cloudflare Workers close to callers, with Postgres for accounts and keys and Redis for rate limits.', '{"slug":"developer-api","title":"API or developer tool that other developers pay to call","summary":"A paid API that developers call with keys: a dashboard where they sign up, create keys and see usage, an API that checks the key and a per-key rate limit on every request, and usage reported to Stripe for metered billing. It runs on Cloudflare Workers close to callers, with Postgres for accounts and keys and Redis for rate limits.","matches":["public api","rest api","graphql api","developer api","api for developers","api product","paid api","developer tool","developer tools","dev tool","devtools","sdk","per api call","api-first"],"fitsWhen":["Customers are developers who call your service from their own code with an API key.","You charge by usage (requests, credits or tokens), by plan with included usage, or both.","Callers are spread out and expect low latency and clear errors."],"notFor":["An internal API that only your own app calls: build it into the app instead.","Long-running jobs behind each request (video, big exports): accept the request, queue the work, and return a job id.","An API that moves or holds money for callers: that needs licensing review first."],"stack":[{"category":"hosting","tool":"cloudflare-workers","why":"The API runs close to callers worldwide with no cold starts to speak of, and Workers Free covers 100,000 requests a day while you find your first customers. Workers caps CPU time per request, which suits fast API calls.","alternatives":[{"tool":"vercel","when":"The API lives next to a Next.js dashboard and you''d rather run one app."}]},{"category":"database","tool":"neon","why":"Accounts, hashed API keys, plans and usage in Postgres, reached from Workers over HTTP with Neon''s serverless driver.","alternatives":[{"tool":"supabase","when":"You want database, auth and storage from one vendor."}]},{"category":"kv","tool":"upstash-redis","why":"Per-key rate limits are a counter on every request; Upstash Redis does atomic increments over HTTP from Workers, and its rate-limit SDK has the windows built in.","alternatives":[{"tool":"cloudflare-durable-objects","when":"You want rate limits inside Cloudflare with no other vendor."}]},{"category":"auth","tool":"clerk","why":"Sign-in for the developer dashboard only; the API itself checks your own API keys, not sessions.","alternatives":[{"tool":"workos-authkit","when":"Customers are companies with teams that need organizations and enterprise SSO."}]},{"category":"payments","tool":"stripe","why":"Metered billing: send each customer''s usage to a Stripe Meter and bill per request or credit, with plans that include a free allowance.","alternatives":[{"tool":"paddle","when":"You sell worldwide and want a merchant of record to handle sales tax and VAT."}]},{"category":"email","tool":"resend","why":"Key-created notices, usage alerts at 80% and 100%, and invoices.","alternatives":[{"tool":"postmark","when":"Transactional deliverability and long retention matter most."}]},{"category":"monitoring","tool":"sentry","why":"Errors and slow requests, tagged with the key''s account (never the key itself).","alternatives":[{"tool":"better-stack","when":"You want uptime checks and a public status page developers can subscribe to."}]},{"category":"jobs","tool":"upstash-qstash","why":"Delivers webhooks to customers'' endpoints with retries and backoff, so a slow customer server doesn''t slow your API.","alternatives":[{"tool":"inngest","when":"Webhooks are part of longer multi-step workflows."}],"optional":true}],"steps":[{"title":"Design the API contract first","detail":"Developers judge an API by its first request, its errors and its docs, and changing a public contract later breaks their code.","actions":["Write an OpenAPI spec for the first endpoints before coding: paths, request and response schemas, and error shapes.","Version from day one (/v1/...) and never change a field''s meaning inside a version.","Use one error format everywhere with a stable code, a message and a link to docs; return 401 for bad keys, 429 with Retry-After for rate limits, 402 or 403 for plan limits.","Make writes safe to retry with an Idempotency-Key header."],"check":"The spec validates, and a developer can tell from it alone how to authenticate, what each endpoint returns and what every error means.","docs":["https://spec.openapis.org/oas/latest.html"]},{"title":"Issue API keys you can show once and revoke anytime","detail":"Store only a hash of each key, show the full key once, and keep a short prefix so developers can tell keys apart.","actions":["Create api_keys (account, name, prefix, sha256 hash, created, last used, revoked) and accounts (plan, Stripe customer id).","Generate keys with a recognizable prefix (for example sk_live_) and 32+ random bytes; show the full key once at creation.","Let developers create, name and revoke keys in the dashboard, with separate test and live keys.","Turn on GitHub secret scanning partner patterns for your prefix later, so leaked keys can be reported to you."],"files":[{"path":"db/001_keys.sql","contents":"create table accounts (\n  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),\n  owner_user_id text not null unique,     -- Clerk user id\n  plan text not null default ''free'',\n  stripe_customer_id text unique,\n  created_at timestamptz not null default now()\n);\n\ncreate table api_keys (\n  id bigserial primary key,\n  account_id uuid not null references accounts(id) on delete cascade,\n  name text not null,\n  prefix text not null,                   -- first 12 characters, shown in the dashboard\n  key_hash text not null unique,          -- sha256 of the full key; the key itself is never stored\n  mode text not null check (mode in (''test'',''live'')),\n  last_used_at timestamptz,\n  revoked_at timestamptz,\n  created_at timestamptz not null default now()\n);\n"},{"path":"src/keys.ts","contents":"const enc = new TextEncoder();\n\nexport async function newKey(mode: \"test\" | \"live\") {\n  const bytes = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32));\n  const key = `sk_${mode}_${btoa(String.fromCharCode(...bytes)).replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, \"\").slice(0, 40)}`;\n  return { key, prefix: key.slice(0, 12), hash: await hashKey(key) };\n}\n\nexport async function hashKey(key: string) {\n  const digest = await crypto.subtle.digest(\"SHA-256\", enc.encode(key));\n  return [...new Uint8Array(digest)].map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\")).join(\"\");\n}\n"}],"check":"A new key works once copied, the database holds only its hash, and a revoked key gets 401 on the next request."},{"title":"Build the API on Workers: check the key, then the rate limit","detail":"Every request does the same two cheap checks before any real work.","actions":["Scaffold a Worker with a small router (Hono works well) and put the key check and rate limit in middleware.","Look up the key by hash; cache valid keys for a short time so most requests skip the database.","Rate-limit per key with a sliding window in Upstash Redis and return 429 with Retry-After and rate-limit headers.","Keep each request fast: Workers caps CPU time per request, so move heavy work to a queue and return a job id."],"commands":["npm create cloudflare@latest my-api -- --framework=hono","npm i @neondatabase/serverless @upstash/ratelimit @upstash/redis"],"files":[{"path":"src/index.ts","contents":"import { Hono } from \"hono\";\nimport { Ratelimit } from \"@upstash/ratelimit\";\nimport { Redis } from \"@upstash/redis/cloudflare\";\nimport { hashKey } from \"./keys\";\nimport { findKey, recordUsage } from \"./db\";\n\ntype Env = { UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL: string; UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN: string; DATABASE_URL: string };\nconst app = new Hono<{ Bindings: Env; Variables: { accountId: string } }>();\n\napp.use(\"/v1/*\", async (c, next) => {\n  const key = c.req.header(\"Authorization\")?.replace(/^Bearer\\s+/, \"\");\n  const row = key ? await findKey(c.env, await hashKey(key)) : null;\n  if (!row || row.revoked_at) return c.json({ error: { code: \"invalid_api_key\", message: \"Missing or invalid API key.\" } }, 401);\n\n  const limiter = new Ratelimit({ redis: Redis.fromEnv(c.env), limiter: Ratelimit.slidingWindow(60, \"1 m\") });\n  const { success, limit, remaining, reset } = await limiter.limit(String(row.id));\n  c.header(\"RateLimit-Limit\", String(limit));\n  c.header(\"RateLimit-Remaining\", String(remaining));\n  if (!success) {\n    c.header(\"Retry-After\", String(Math.ceil((reset - Date.now()) / 1000)));\n    return c.json({ error: { code: \"rate_limited\", message: \"Too many requests.\" } }, 429);\n  }\n  c.set(\"accountId\", row.account_id);\n  await next();\n  c.executionCtx.waitUntil(recordUsage(c.env, row.account_id, row.id)); // count after responding\n});\n\napp.get(\"/v1/hello\", (c) => c.json({ ok: true }));\n\nexport default app;\n"}],"check":"A request with no key gets 401, the 61st request in a minute gets 429 with Retry-After, and a normal request answers in under 100 ms from a nearby region.","docs":["https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/","https://upstash.com/docs/redis/sdks/ratelimit-ts/overview","https://neon.com/docs/serverless/serverless-driver"]},{"title":"Count usage and bill it through Stripe","detail":"Count every billable request cheaply, then send totals to Stripe in batches, never one call per request.","actions":["Increment a per-account, per-day usage counter after each billable request (Redis or a usage table).","Create a Stripe Meter and a metered price; from a scheduled job, report each account''s new usage with an identifier per batch so retries don''t double-bill.","Give the free plan an allowance and enforce it on the server with a clear 402 or 403 error and an upgrade link.","Show usage to date and the projected invoice in the dashboard."],"commands":["npm i stripe"],"check":"A test account''s requests show on its Stripe invoice preview within a day, and the free allowance blocks requests past its limit with an upgrade link.","docs":["https://docs.stripe.com/billing/subscriptions/usage-based","https://stripe.com/billing/pricing"]},{"title":"Build the developer dashboard","detail":"Sign-up to first successful request should take a couple of minutes.","actions":["Sign in with Clerk; create the account and a test key on first sign-in.","Show a copy-paste curl request with the developer''s test key filled in, and the response it returns.","Pages for keys, usage by day, plan and billing (Stripe customer portal), and webhooks if you send them."],"check":"A new developer can sign up, copy the sample request and get a 200 from your API in under two minutes.","docs":["https://clerk.com/docs"]},{"title":"Publish docs and an SDK","detail":"Generate reference docs from the OpenAPI spec so they never drift from the API.","actions":["Publish reference docs generated from the spec, plus a quickstart and an errors page that every error links to.","Generate a TypeScript (and Python, if your users want it) client from the spec, or write a thin one.","Add an llms.txt and plain-text docs so coding agents can read them.","Keep a changelog and announce deprecations with dates before removing anything."],"check":"Every endpoint in the spec appears in the docs with a working example, and the SDK''s example runs against the test key.","docs":["https://llmstxt.org"]},{"title":"Send webhooks with signatures and retries","detail":"If customers need to know when something happens, sign each webhook and retry failures without blocking your API.","actions":["Let developers register endpoint URLs and give each one a signing secret.","Sign the body with HMAC-SHA256 and a timestamp, and document how to verify it.","Deliver through QStash so failed deliveries retry with backoff; every retry counts as a message.","Show recent deliveries and their responses in the dashboard so developers can debug."],"commands":["npm i @upstash/qstash"],"check":"A webhook to an endpoint that fails twice is delivered on the third try, and the receiving code can verify its signature.","docs":["https://upstash.com/docs/qstash/overall/getstarted"]},{"title":"Launch with monitoring and a status page","detail":"Developers notice errors and latency before you do, so watch both and tell them when something''s wrong.","actions":["Add Sentry to the Worker; tag errors with account id, never the API key or request body.","Track error rate and p95 latency per endpoint, and alert on both.","Publish a status page and an email or RSS feed for incidents.","Move to Workers Paid ($5/month) before launch if 10 ms of CPU per request is too little or you''ll pass 100,000 requests a day."],"check":"You can see error rate and p95 latency per endpoint for the last day, and a test incident shows on the status page.","docs":["https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/cloudflare/","https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/"]}],"bestPractices":["Store only a hash of each API key, show it once, and let developers revoke it.","Check the key and the rate limit before any real work on every request.","Version the API and never change a field''s meaning inside a version.","Use one error format with stable codes, and return Retry-After on 429.","Batch usage reports to Stripe with idempotent identifiers; never report per request.","Generate docs and SDKs from the OpenAPI spec so they match the API."],"pitfalls":["Storing API keys in plain text, so one database leak exposes every customer.","Reporting usage to Stripe on every request, which is slow and fails under load.","Rate-limiting per IP instead of per key, so one customer''s servers block each other.","Doing heavy work inside the request on Workers and hitting the CPU limit.","Breaking response shapes without a new version and breaking customers'' code.","Logging full request bodies or keys in error reports."],"complianceNotes":["Publish API terms covering acceptable use, rate limits, uptime promises (if any) and what you do with data sent to the API.","If callers send personal data through the API, you''re likely their data processor: offer a data processing agreement and list your vendors.","Keep logs of key creation, revocation and admin actions; enterprise customers will ask in security reviews."],"catches":[{"text":"Workers Free allows 100,000 requests a day and 10 ms of CPU time per request; plan to move to Workers Paid ($5/month) before launch if your requests do more work than that.","source":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/","verifiedOn":"2026-11-09"},{"text":"Upstash Redis Free covers 500K commands a month. A rate-limit check is a few commands, so the free plan runs out around a couple hundred thousand API calls a month; after that it''s pay as you go.","source":"https://upstash.com/pricing/redis","verifiedOn":"2026-11-07"},{"text":"Metered billing on Stripe adds Stripe Billing''s 0.7% of billing volume on top of card fees.","source":"https://stripe.com/pricing","verifiedOn":"2026-11-07"},{"text":"If you deliver webhooks through QStash, every delivery attempt counts as a message, so retries to a failing customer endpoint add to the bill; Free stops at 1,000 messages a day.","source":"https://upstash.com/pricing/qstash","verifiedOn":"2026-11-20"}],"costNotes":["Hosting: Workers Free covers 100,000 requests a day; Workers Paid is $5/month when you need more CPU per request or more requests.","Rate limits: about 3 Redis commands per request × 100,000 requests a month = 300K commands, inside Upstash Free''s 500K; past that, $0.20 per 100K.","Card fees on what you bill: 2.9% + 30¢ per charge, plus 0.7% of billing volume for Stripe Billing."],"verifiedOn":"2026-11-20"}'::jsonb, '2026-11-20')
